In Fig.\,\ref{fig:tmid_rp30}, we show the midplane and sublimation temperature for different planet masses ($\Mp$) at $\rp=30\,$au for the \md\ case. Since $\Mp=10\Me$ is unable to open a deep gap, the temperature profile is similar to the smooth disk. As $\Mp$ increases, the gap region becomes hotter, which is consistent with the results in \citetalias{chen_planet_2023}. 
