Next, if $\pi<t_2-t_1\leq 2\pi$ then,   according to \cite[Theorem 1.2]{MS}, the corresponding contact structure, denoted by $\xi_{ot1}$, is obtained by performing a half-Lutz twist to $\xi_t$.  
%The corresponding moment cone is defined by the rays $(1,0)$ and $(-l,-k).$
% that is, the angle between the rays is equal to $t_{k,l}+\pi.$ 
   By performing a sequence of full-Lutz twists to $\xi_{ot1}$ we obtain isotopic overtwisted contact structure, with a different toric action. 
   The corresponding moment cone is defined by the same rays $(1,0)$ and
    $(-l,-k),$ however, the angle between the rays increases by $2n\pi ,$  where $n$ is the number of performed full-Lutz twists to $\xi_{ot1}$. 
   If $2\pi<t_2-t_1\leq 3\pi$ then the corresponding contact structure, denoted by $  \xi_{ot2}$  is obtained by performing a full-Lutz twist to $  \xi_t,$ or, by performing a half-Lutz twist to $ \xi_{ot1}.$
