\subsection{Contact  3-manifolds with a non-free toric action}
We first prove theorem for  the tight contact toric structures and then for overtwisted ones.


\noindent \textbf{1. Case} If $t_2-t_1=\pi$ the corresponding contact toric manifold is equivariantly contactomorphic to $S^1 \times S^2$ with the unique tight contact structure $\xi_t$ and the moment cone shown on the right in Figure \ref{fig:lens}.
By a simple computation that relies on (\ref{eq:rays}), we conclude that this  contact toric structure  can be realised as
a concave contact boundary of the  linear plumbings
         $$(n,0,-n), n  \geq0,$$
         with a symplectic toric structure shown on the left in Figure 9.   
           Since equivariant symplectomorphisms preserve self-intersection numbers of spheres corresponding to edges in the moment map image, it follows that these plumbings are mutually not equivariantly symplectomorphic.




