Recall $\bm{l}$ in (\ref{eq_originaldefinition}) which involves both $t \in [0,1]$ and $x \in \mathbb{R}$. The Gaussian approximation result, Theorem \ref{thm_gaussianapproximationcase}, provides controls on the following Kolmogorov distance {for any given fixed $t$ and $x$
\begin{equation*}
\mathcal{K}(\bm{z}, \bm{v}):=\sup_{\mathsf{x} \in \mathbb{R}} \left| \mathbb{P}( \bm{z}^\top \bm{l} \leq \mathsf{x})-\mathbb{P}(  \bm{v}^\top \bm{l} \leq \mathsf{x}) \right|,
