\textit{\textbf{Change of strain:}}\\
We examine the variation of strain $e_{33}$ against $y_3$ on the aseismic period after critical time $T$ through figure \ref{figure8}. The magnitude of change of strain is found to be in the order of $10^{-8}$, which confirms the strain rate value studied by Michael (2005). A significant change in strain is observed around a depth of $10,000$ m below the free surface, where the fault is situated. The strain is maximum at $y_3=11,100$ m, which is approximately $2.278\times 10^{-8}$ beyond which the strain $e_{33}$ gradually returns towards zero. Such behaviour could indicate a strain concentration or a localized deformation zone within the material.
