The calculations are performed for a single self-assembled InGaAs/GaAs QD. We represent the QDs geometry by the dome shape of height $h$ and the radius $r$. The dot is placed on a wetting layer of thickness $a$ (the single lattice constant). The material distribution is presented in Fig.~\ref{fig:comp_map}. For simplicity, we assume a constant In$_x$Ga$_{1-x}$As distribution (denoted as $x_\mathrm{QD}$) in the QD and in the wetting layer. To take into account the material intermixing at the interfaces, the initial composition is processed by the Gaussian blur with the standard deviation of $a$.

