Using Pappus' and Desargues' theorems it can be shown, that for the such defined addition and product of points the associative, commutative, and distributive law is valid. This, in turn, means that in the Schwabh\"{a}user-Szmielew-Tarski system, we must first prove the Poppus theorem, and on its basis, the Desargues theorem, which is not so easy.
