			commutes by naturality of the family $\set{\Gamma}$ with respect to $\Gamma_h*x$ and by axiom (b) of a colax algebra (see Definition \ref{def:colax-algebra}). Therefore, $(\bar\Gamma_h)_x = (\Gamma_h)_x$, which entails that $\bar \Gamma = \Gamma$.

			For a pair of functors $h \colon J b \to C, k \colon J c \to T b$, the natural transformation $\bar\Delta_{h,k}$ is defined at an object $\nu\in T c$ as the composite
			\[ \begin{tikzcd}
