For upward drives used in the experiments shown in Figure \ref{YZs}, a comparison is made between the disk's center-of-mass position C and that simulated  both by the full equations, (\ref{eq:YZeqs}) and(\ref{angmom4}),  as well as by the simplified set, represented by the DLE (\ref{eq:DLEQ}). This  comparison will be done both in physical $YZ$-space as well as in the three-dimensional $\mathcal{J} YZ$-phase space, which, interestingly, embeds physical space.  

