Suppose that $B\subseteq A$ for some $B\in\mathcal J$. Since $A\cap [t]=\emptyset$, we have that $B\in\widehat{\mathcal J}$, which is a contradiction.

Finally, suppose that there exist $W,X,Y\in\mathcal I$ and $Z\subsetneq A$ such that $W,X,Y, Z$ form a diamond with $Z$ being its top element, as depicted below.
