\subsubsection{\texorpdfstring{$\phi$-$X$-$Z$}{phi-X-Z} correlator system: obtaining an island without symmetry enhancement}
We have thus far learnt that the $Z$-$X$ system is capable of preventing symmetry enhancement, and that the $\phi$-$Z$ system is capable of producing and island. Thus, studying a $\phi$-$X$-$Z$ mixed correlator system should be sufficient to produce an island that does not include in it the $O(3)$ fixed point. In Fig.\ \ref{fig:PhiXZLambda19Channel}, we see that this is indeed the case. This figure corresponds to a two-dimensional slice of a larger three-dimensional island we have obtained. This slice is taken precisely at the value of $\Delta_\phi$ that corresponds to the $O(3)$ fixed point, i.e.\ $\Delta_\phi=0.51893$ \cite{Chester:2020iyt}.

