All of this is done so we can now perform the \emph{symmetric capping operation} introduced in \cite[2.3]{freedman_quinn_1990} using the resulting two discs $D_A$, $D_B$. To do so, we remove a neighbourhood of $\partial_A \cup \partial_B$ from $T$ and glue back two parallel copies of $D_A$, two parallel copies of $D_B$ and glue back in a square in $T$ around $\partial D_A \cap \partial D_B \in T$ to fill the resulting hole (see Figure \ref{figure:symmetric_capping}). 
