Note that $P$ is an \emph{immersed} sphere with double points. Moreover, as of now $P$ intersects $W$ in more than one point---we did introduce more intersections during our operations.
However, we can remove the extra intersections between $W$ and $P$ as follows. Start with those between $D_B$ and $W$. Push down all such intersections into $T$ so that the intersection points of $W$ and $T$ lie on $\partial D_A$. Now when we perform symmetric capping to get $P$, $W$ will not intersect $P$ in there (see Figure \ref{figure:removingIntersections}). Same can be done for intersections between $D_A$ and $W$. 
