% Such correlations, in accordance with the rotational model, need to be confirmed by experimental data.
A similar result of  $Q_{_S}(2_{_1}^+)\approx0.06$ eb is  determined by other {\it ab initio}~\cite{epelbaum2012structure,dreyfuss2013hoyle,forssen2013systematics,d2020precision} and
theoretical approaches~\cite{abgrall1972multipole,bassel19820+}, including
shell-model ({\sc SM}) calculations using the Cohen-Kurath
% (1965)
interaction~\cite{cohen1965effective}
% also yields $Q_{_S}(2_{_1}^+)=0.064$ eb~\cite{bassel19820+}, without uncertainties,
% already accepted a missing degree of collectivity in the restricted basis of the model
% especially knowing the relatively slow convergence of {\it ab initio} B($\hat{E2}$) calculations requiring a large model space which is computationally demanding task.
and admixtures outside the $p-$shell from the isoscalar giant quadrupole resonance~\cite{bassel19820+}.
Lastly, Monte Carlo lattice calculations~\cite{epelbaum2012structure} and cluster  models~\cite{marin2014evidence,freer2018microscopic,kanada2007structure,chernykh2007structure} predict an oblate shaped 2$_{_1}^+$ state in $^{12}$C, with a compact triangular three-$\alpha$ cluster and mean-field admixtures.
