\begin{proposition}
A non-negative integer $6 \times 6$ matrix $M$ is the CN matrix of some pure $6$-braid projection if and only if $M$ is an even symmetric T0 matrix. 
\label{prop-CN6}
\end{proposition}

\begin{proof}
If a matrix $M$ is CN-realizable by a pure braid projection, then $M$ is symmetric by definition and $M$ is a non-negative even T0 matrix by Propositions \ref{prop-pure-even} and \ref{prop-T0}. 
